{"name":"Alton Brown","hex":"#5a464b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alton Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Alton Crawford Brown Jr. is an American television personality, food show presenter, author, voice actor, YouTuber, and cinematographer. He is the creator and host of the Food Network television show Good Eats that ran for 16 seasons, host of the miniseries Feasting on Asphalt and Feasting on Waves, and host and main commentator on Iron Chef America and Cutthroat Kitchen. Brown is a best-selling author of several books on food and cooking. A recap series titled Good Eats Reloaded aired on Cooking Channel, and a true sequel series, Good Eats: The Return, ran from 2019 to 2021 on Food Network."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Alton_Brown_Hopelink_4_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Alton_Brown_Hopelink_4_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alton_Brown","wikidata":"Q4736872"},{"title":"Alton Brown (baseball)","blocks":[{"text":"Alton Leo \"Deacon\" Brown was an American right-handed Major League Baseball relief pitcher who played for the Washington Senators in 1951."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/ff/Alton_Brown_%28baseball%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alton_Brown_(baseball)","wikidata":"Q4736869"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely 